Subject: [parser] Fix spread errors in async() calls inside async arrow params

In ParserBase::ParseArguments, record rest-parameter errors
(kRestDefaultInitializer and kParamAfterRest) using
RecordDeclarationError on the current ArrowHeadParsingScope rather than
RecordAsyncArrowParametersError. Those errors apply only to the current
arrow head if it turns out to be an arrow parameter list, not to
enclosing async arrow heads when the current call turns out to be a
normal 'async(...)' call expression.

Also check the scope chain flags on the walked scope rather than 'this'
in RecordAsyncArrowParametersError and RecordParameterInitializerError.

Bug: 567222737
TAG=agy
CONV=905f9f91-322f-467a-9f81-1f78a365b0d8

